@page "/staff/help"
@layout paa_frontend.Client.Layout.StaffPortalLayout
<div class="help-page"><h1>Staff help centre</h1><p class="lead">A practical guide to the staff portal.</p><section><h2>Dashboard</h2><p>Use the dashboard for a quick view of your classes, recent activity, and tasks that need attention.</p></section><section><h2>Students</h2><p>Find a learner, open their profile, and check the information needed for teaching and attendance. Confirm the learner before recording anything.</p></section><section><h2>Marks</h2><p>Choose the correct class, subject, term, and year before entering marks. Enter the mark using the assessment’s maximum score, review the totals, then submit. Existing assessments can be edited when the system allows it; always check the term and year before saving.</p><p>Submitted marks may need administrator approval before students can see them.</p></section><section><h2>Attendance</h2><p>Select the correct date and class, mark each learner carefully, and save once. Correct mistakes as soon as possible and tell administration if the date is wrong.</p></section><section><h2>Profile and troubleshooting</h2><p>Keep your profile details current. If a list is empty, check your filters and term/year, refresh once, and contact administration if the problem continues.</p></section></div><style>.help-page{max-width:900px;margin:32px auto;padding:0 20px;color:#0f172a}.help-page h1{font-size:32px;margin:0 0 8px}.lead{color:#64748b;margin-bottom:26px}.help-page section{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:18px;padding:20px;margin:14px 0;box-shadow:0 4px 14px #0f172a0a}.help-page h2{font-size:18px;margin:0 0 8px}.help-page p{line-height:1.65;color:#475569}</style>
